; Optics whose lens the bodycam reference glass blanks. While one of these is
; aimed, zzz_bodycam_scope_effects_guard turns bodycam scope effects off, and
; turns them back on when you lower the weapon or switch to any other optic.
;
; Why these: the reference image is only presented on the deferred-glass path,
; and NV / thermal / digital-display optics are excluded from deferred glass by
; design (svp_optics.cpp: !(scope_glass_deferred_current() && ps_r2_nightvision)).
; Confirmed broken by measurement on 1pn93 and echo1; pn23 reported by Walter.
; The rest are every other runtime section in pip_optic_physical_specs.ltx bound
; to a spec whose optic_class is display or night_vision_display - the same
; family, rather than a guess per weapon.
;
; Names match CWeapon:GetScopeName() first, then the weapon's own section,
; either exactly, as an underscore-separated token, or as a trailing _<name>.
; That last form is what catches integrated optics, which report no scope name
; at all (measured: "scope= diagnostic_scope=1pn93" for wpn_ak101_1pn93).
;
; This list is MINIMAL: 10 further entries were dropped because the names below
; already matched every section they did - wpn_m98b_pn23 is caught by pn23,
; wpn_k98_mod_skeet by skeet, and so on. Verified over all 7030 weapon and
; up_sect sections in this install: 431/431 of the listed-optic variants match,
; with zero false positives. Re-check after adding one, since a short name can
; catch more than you intend.
;
; Add or remove freely - one name per line, value ignored. If an optic in here
; turns out to render fine, delete it and you keep the bodycam glass on it.

; MAGNIFIER HYBRIDS, added 2026-10-29. These are NOT display optics - they bind
; geometric specs (optic_eotech_g33_3x, optic_sig_juliet6_6x24) and are the
; hybrid reflex-plus-magnifier class from pip_hybrid_optics.ltx. They show the
; same blank lens, so the breakage is wider than the display class alone.
;
; Confirmed on the EOTech EXPS + FTC magnifier (e0t2_magd) on the AR15 Viper 2.
; uh1_magd is the same class and is included on that basis, not tested.
;
; The _off rows cover the flipped-away state, where the optic is an unmagnified
; reflex. If that state renders FINE for you with scope effects on, delete the
; two _off lines and you keep the bodycam glass on the reflex, which is where it
; looks best. Left in because a blank lens is worse than a missing effect.
;
; Twelve more hybrid sections exist in pip_hybrid_optics.ltx (exps3_mag,
; exps3_magd, romeo8_magd, romeo4_magd, he510_magd and their variants) and are
; deliberately NOT listed: they match no weapon section in this install, so they
; would be dead entries. Add them if a weapon pack later brings them in.

; mode decides what the hold keys off.
;
;   pip    Hold bodycam scope effects off whenever PiP scopes are ON
;          (r__svpscope is 1 or 2), for every optic. This is the default.
;          The cvar is re-read as you aim, so r__svpscope 0 gives the bodycam
;          glass back live and setting it to 1 or 2 takes it away again, with
;          no restart.
;
;   list   Hold them off only for the optics in [broken_optics] below.
;          That is the targeted behaviour, for when you want the bodycam glass
;          on everything that renders it correctly.
;
; Either way the setting is restored the moment you lower the weapon, so the
; Modded Exes menu still shows scope effects enabled and nothing else in
; bodycam sees it change. A value you set to off yourself is left alone.
[settings]
mode = pip

[broken_optics]
e0t2_magd
e0t2_magd_off
e0t2_magd_unity
e0t2_magd_unity_off
uh1_magd
uh1_magd_off
1pn93
1pn93n2_1gs
echo1
gauss_sight
pn23
skeet
t12
up_sect_firsta_binoc
up_sect_firstc_binoc
up_sect_firste_binoc
vulcan
wpn_g36c_rwap
wpn_gauss
wpn_gauss_quest
